    "html": "\r\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\r\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\r\n    <span class=\"time\">35 min</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Interview Hub</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Company lists</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Premium data</span>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <h1>Company coding patterns</h1>\r\n  <p class=\"lead\">What Google, Meta, Amazon, Microsoft, Flipkart, Walmart, Uber and a dozen others actually ask in coding rounds, measured from the saved Premium company lists (frequency 1-8 per problem) and 1,883 questions named in 2024-26 interview posts. You get each company's favourite patterns, difficulty mix and round style, two templates for the problems they love most, and a plan for using the company filters in the last weeks before a loop.</p>\r\n  <p class=\"small prereq\"><b>Before this page:</b> <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-sheets-guide\">Which sheet to use</a> (how the Dojo 450 is built). <b>Also:</b> the company guides for the full loop, e.g. <a href=\"{{BASE}}companies/co-meta\">Meta</a>, <a href=\"{{BASE}}companies/co-amazon\">Amazon</a>, <a href=\"{{BASE}}companies/co-google\">Google</a>.</p>\r\n",
